<title>AUSTRALIA: Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - May 19.</title>
<headline>Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - May 19.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	 348.39   7.56</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	   229.17   1.10</p>
<p> 3   Ranger Minerals	193.78   4.05</p>
<p> 4   Perilya Mines	  181.40   0.78</p>
<p> 5   Syd Hrbr Casino	150.68   2.23</p>
<p> 6   Equatorial Min	 133.33   0.24</p>
<p> 7   Westpac Prop Tr	107.50   1.72</p>
<p> 8   St.Barbara Mine	 90.14   0.64</p>
<p> 9   Tap Oil		   82.95   1.46</p>
<p>10   Consol Paper	    80.29   2.73</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Climax Mining	    2.08   1.03</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	    4.46   1.00</p>
<p> 3   Jardine Fm China	 5.10   0.76</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		    5.70   5.30</p>
<p> 5   Premier Inv		5.94   1.40</p>
<p> 6   Adel Bton Cement	 7.26   1.74</p>
<p> 7   OLS Asia Hldgs	   7.33   1.05</p>
<p> 8   BT Aust Eq Mgmt	  7.62   0.77</p>
<p> 9   Renison Goldflds	 7.70   5.25</p>
<p>10   FAI Life ltd	     7.75   0.77</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
